        <div class="insight-text">Excess kurtosis of 7.02 (vs. 0 for a normal distribution) means gold's tail losses occur far more frequently than Gaussian models predict. A portfolio using normal-distribution VaR will underestimate 1% tail risk by ~22%. Use t-distribution (ν≈5–7) or EVT-based approaches for stress-testing gold positions.</div>
